  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Jesus Children** (1 other source): Played as a sandwich: Jesus Children into Who Knows, then back into Jesus Children [1]\n- **So Live!** (1 other source): Ryan Zoidas of Rustic Overtones sat in on this song, along with Steppin and Cannonball marked with asterisks [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Shuman**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n- **World Is A Ghetto**: rare: 14 archived performances [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2000-10-21.shnf** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 15 songs; 107 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer recalls the matrix recording's sound quality as above average and calls it a keeper; Minor flaws: a splice before Doin' Something, a odd vocal glitch before Cannonball, and a fade between discs one and two [1][2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The Stone Coast room was extremely hot that night because the ventilation system was broken [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2000-10-21.shnf**: taped by Pete Costello; transferred by Andrew Land/Eric McRoberts; source: matrix: (On Stage) Schoeps cmc621(on 4' pole, 90 degrees, 50%)+sbd(@50%)->Mackie 1202 vlz->Apogee AD-1000(+4dB, @44.1kHz) [1]",
